# TEST FIXTURE CORPORA (#7927). These are test INPUT DATA, not documentation, and
# linting them is a category error: the linter rewrites the very bytes a suite asserts
# on. Both failure modes were measured on this branch, not anticipated.
#
#   - plugins/soleur/test/fixtures/ship-incident-pir-gate/ is the corpus for a
#     paragraph/heading BOUNDARY classifier, so its blank lines ARE the input. MD012's
#     two added blank lines flipped rows M5 and M9 from want=no to got=yes: 25/25 with
#     main's fixtures, 23/25 with the swept ones.
#   - test/helpers/sample-content.md is asserted on by substring. The MD034 autolink
#     rewrite turned `Link: https://...` into `Link: <https://...` and broke
#     content-publisher's extraction assertion.
#
# A fixture is only lint-clean by coincidence; a suite that depends on its bytes is not.
# Documentation that happens to live under a fixture directory (a README explaining the
# corpus) stays in scope deliberately -- test/fixtures/orphan-proc-dangling/README.md is
# the reason the `test` root still appears in EXPECTED_ROOTS.
